What I Learned Building This

This project gave me hands-on experience with the complete RAG pipeline — from converting raw documents into vector embeddings, to storing them in a persistent vector database, to retrieving semantically relevant chunks at query time, to constructing structured prompts for an LLM, and finally generating grounded answers with source attribution.
I also learned the importance of score thresholding in production RAG systems. Without a minimum similarity threshold, the retriever can return completely unrelated documents which causes the LLM to generate inaccurate or hallucinated answers. Setting a proper threshold is one of the most important tuning decisions in any RAG pipeline.

